fork`+`waitpid` signal.\n- **Phase D**: symbol diff empty; no `[features]` table exists (verified mechanically), so `run_tests.sh` enumerates it and runs default + `--no-default-features` × `dev`/`release`. No binary target exists (`add_library` only, no `main`), so the binary-stdout gate is N/A.\n\n## Harness trustworthiness\nBoth libraries are loaded only via `libloading` and called through their exports. A negative control injected 11 deliberate Rust bugs — 10 were caught (2–21 failing tests each). The 11th (deleting the `errno == 0` conjunct) is a proven **equivalent mutant**: on LP64 glibc `ERANGE` always coincides with out-of-`int` range, measured and documented in `ERRORS.md`.\n\n`c_src/` sources are unmodified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":403,"cache_read_input_tokens":96576,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":403,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8bc26632-7b3e-45a2-bf4d-5cf018bc1bab","uuid":"b8afa33d-d826-4177-bb70-d6ecc810b94c","timestamp":"2026-09-05T04:10:03.890Z"}
